# the per-channel addressing the repack produces, shown against the same
# model emitted WITHOUT SEQ_REPACK (both SEQ_NCH=4, 16 images, 7000-row head)
#
#   tok7k_flat  repack=False  per-channel tops 0x118ce600 x4   busiest 24.81 MiB
#     head MVGOs: (0,0x114f6000) (1,0x11616000) (2,0x11736000) (3,0x11856000)
#                 = base + GLOBAL row {0,2048,4096,6144} * stride
#
#   tok7k       repack=True   per-channel tops 0x1065e000 0x1065e000
#                                              0x1065e000 0x105b6600
#                                              busiest  6.37 MiB  (3.9x less)
#     head MVGOs: (0,0x1053e000) (1,0x1053e000) (2,0x1053e000) (3,0x1053e000)
#                 = each channel's OWN base + packed row 0, holding global
#                   rows 0..2047 / 2048..4095 / 4096..6143 / 6144..6999
#                   (2048/2048/2048/856 rows — an UNEVEN ILV split)
#
# The gate above is what proves the second reading is the right one: the
# golden resolves each per-channel address back to those global rows and
# reproduces the .txt state bit-for-bit.
